meta {
  name: get voices list
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{url}}/api/voices/list
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "voiceType": "edge-tts"
  }
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
}

docs {
  # Get Voices List
  
  Retrieve all available voices for a specific voice type.
  
  ## Endpoint
  POST /api/voices/list
  
  ## Authentication
  Not required
  
  ## Request Body
  ```json
  {
    "voiceType": "edge-tts"
  }
  ```
  
  - `voiceType`: Currently only "edge-tts" is supported
  
  ## Description
  Returns a list of all Microsoft Edge TTS voices supporting multiple languages, 
  countries, and genders.
  
  ## Response (201 Created)
  ```json
  {
    "voiceType": "edge-tts",
    "voices": [
      {
        "id": "th-TH-NiwatNeural",
        "language": "th-TH",
        "gender": "Male",
        "name": "Microsoft Niwat Online (Natural) - Thai (Thailand)"
      },
      {
        "id": "th-TH-PremwadeeNeural",
        "language": "th-TH",
        "gender": "Female",
        "name": "Microsoft Premwadee Online (Natural) - Thai (Thailand)"
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
  
  - `id`: Voice ID to use in generate dubbing requests
  - `language`: Language code (ISO format, e.g., "th-TH", "en-US")
  - `gender`: Voice gender ("Male" or "Female")
  - `name`: Full descriptive name of the voice
  
  ## Error Responses
  - **400 Bad Request**: `voiceType` is required or invalid
  
  ## Use Cases
  - Display voice selection options to users
  - Filter voices by language
  - Filter voices by gender
  - Get voice ID for dubbing generation
}

